<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rdf:RDF
    xml:base="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/"
    xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
    xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
    xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
    xmlns:ont="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/">

    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/">
        <rdfs:label>agent-bios service routes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>The six paths the service actually runs, in call order. Edges are SEQUENCE, not obligation, and the label carries the route and step number. Colour is ROUTE COUNT — pale slate on one route, purple on two, magenta on three or more; a darker node is a step where one change lands on several routes. Entities on no declared route are omitted; the obligation view carries them.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>

    <!-- Steps -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/InstructionsRule">
        <rdfs:label>InstructionsRule</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An instruction bullet identified by its source anchor; selected always-surface rules enter explicitly activated private sessions. On 4 route(s): author-to-deployed, learn-loop, legacy-install, instruction-import; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Guide">
        <rdfs:label>Guide</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A scoped instruction document exposed by the selected session router and loaded when relevant. On 1 route(s): author-to-deployed; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>▸</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#A8B4C0</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PackagingTier">
        <rdfs:label>PackagingTier</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>core, domain, env-personal or infra — decides whether a unit is universal, opt-in, or plumbing. On 1 route(s): author-to-deployed; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>▸</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#A8B4C0</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Domain">
        <rdfs:label>Domain</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An opt-in bundle of instruction content declared in the domain manifest. On 1 route(s): author-to-deployed; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>▸</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#A8B4C0</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PayloadEntry">
        <rdfs:label>PayloadEntry</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A shipped path declared by package.json files[] and checked against real runtime references. On 1 route(s): author-to-deployed; guard derived</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>▸</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#A8B4C0</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/CliSubcommand">
        <rdfs:label>CliSubcommand</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A user-invocable operation with a named command owner; install/onboard default to terminal setup while JSON setup serves reviewed conversation installation through the same controller, reached from a public repository-link request or an installed skill. On 10 route(s): install, uninstall, learn-loop, migrate, reset, shell-connection, setup, instruction-import, app-context, conversation_setup; guard unguarded</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/DeployTarget">
        <rdfs:label>DeployTarget</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A bounded owned write: private releases and launcher projections, an explicitly registered app discovery link, or native instructions destinations on the compatibility route. On 5 route(s): install, legacy-install, migrate, reset, app-context; guard partial</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Selection">
        <rdfs:label>Selection</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Saved or invocation-local none/default/selected policies and qualified targets, reviewed through SetupController and its UI; imported host/project scope constrains delivery. On 5 route(s): install, session-activation, setup, app-context, conversation_setup; guard unguarded</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/InstructionsAssembler">
        <rdfs:label>InstructionsAssembler</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Compiles selected items into immutable snapshots for native session adapters or explicit app context; reviewed imports publish private personal items through the same store. On 5 route(s): install, legacy-install, session-activation, instruction-import, app-context; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/StateArtifact">
        <rdfs:label>StateArtifact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Persisted private sources, import evidence and receipts, baselines, immutable snapshots, native pins, app context receipts, setup review/outcome receipts and transaction journals; each has owning writers and readers. On 9 route(s): install, uninstall, legacy-install, session-activation, reset, setup, instruction-import, app-context, conversation_setup; guard partial</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/DeploymentManifest">
        <rdfs:label>DeploymentManifest</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Ownership records for removal: private installation metadata, shell receipts and exact app bridge generations; legacy deployment uses manifest.txt. On 6 route(s): install, uninstall, legacy-install, legacy-uninstall, shell-connection, app-context; guard unguarded</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Gate">
        <rdfs:label>Gate</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An executable check owning an invariant, a subject set and an enforcement claim. On 3 route(s): install, legacy-install, instruction-import; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/ShellInterception">
        <rdfs:label>ShellInterception</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An optional zero-argument launcher entry, with receipt-backed shell restore/remove and a shared zsh adapter. On 6 route(s): uninstall, launch, legacy-install, legacy-uninstall, reset, shell-connection; guard partial</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/LearningRecord">
        <rdfs:label>LearningRecord</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An immutable session learning event validated and scrubbed by the collector, stored privately and projected into later selected snapshots. On 3 route(s): learn-loop, legacy-install, migrate; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/SessionDistillPipeline">
        <rdfs:label>SessionDistillPipeline</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>The heavy curator flow that mines many sessions into instructions-grade items. On 1 route(s): learn-loop; guard partial</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>▸</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#A8B4C0</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PresetMode">
        <rdfs:label>PresetMode</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>software-engineer, builder or distill, plus the user-owned presets.local.toml. On 2 route(s): launch, legacy-install; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#7719AA</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/TierBinding">
        <rdfs:label>TierBinding</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>(host, tier) to (model, effort), with display names derived from the launch profile model_display map. On 2 route(s): launch, legacy-install; guard partial</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#7719AA</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Host">
        <rdfs:label>Host</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A model family seat; the provider reverse map must be unique to resolve one validatable seat. On 3 route(s): launch, review-dispatch, session-activation; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Backend">
        <rdfs:label>Backend</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>The CLI actually executed, with its passthrough arguments. On 2 route(s): launch, session-activation; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#7719AA</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/ReviewMethod">
        <rdfs:label>ReviewMethod</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A named way to obtain a review, with perspectives, trials and a severity map. On 1 route(s): review-dispatch; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>▸</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#A8B4C0</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Capability">
        <rdfs:label>Capability</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An optional external tool; data-only, so no resolver branch reads its identity. On 2 route(s): review-dispatch, legacy-install; guard gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#7719AA</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Wrapper">
        <rdfs:label>Wrapper</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An internal dispatch script loaded from the selected package; explicit legacy installation also deploys wrapper copies. On 2 route(s): review-dispatch, legacy-install; guard unguarded</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#7719AA</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/HostPrerequisite">
        <rdfs:label>HostPrerequisite</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Locally probed host tools and interpreters; explicit setup offers available fixed installation commands, while manual account/configuration steps remain separate. On 3 route(s): legacy-install, setup, conversation_setup; guard unguarded</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Migration">
        <rdfs:label>Migration</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An explicit transform of owned legacy state into private state, with pinned release authority and replayable cleanup; compatibility installer migrations remain on their selected route. On 3 route(s): legacy-install, legacy-uninstall, migrate; guard unguarded</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Hook">
        <rdfs:label>Hook</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>An event instruction with a canonical carrier and manifest binding, compiled into host-specific session hooks when native consumption is selected. On 1 route(s): legacy-install; guard partial</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>▸</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#A8B4C0</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/UserOwnedFileRegion">
        <rdfs:label>UserOwnedFileRegion</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A bounded managed span or discovery entry in user-owned native state: optional shell wiring and explicit app bridge registration; globals remain preserved outside explicit legacy cleanup. On 4 route(s): legacy-install, legacy-uninstall, migrate, shell-connection; guard partial</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#E3008C</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/ManagedRuntime">
        <rdfs:label>ManagedRuntime</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment>A supplied Python dependency environment: verified shipped UI wheels loaded into a process-owned temporary directory on package CLI paths, with separately retained managed/numbered compatibility clients. On 2 route(s): legacy-install, setup; guard partial</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:icon>🔀</ont:icon>
        <ont:color>#7719AA</ont:color>
    </owl:Class>

    <!-- Route sequences -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/instructions-rule_entityId">
        <rdfs:label>entityId</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/InstructionsRule"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>instructions-rule</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:isIdentifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ont:isIdentifier>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/instructions-rule_routes">
        <rdfs:label>routes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/InstructionsRule"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>author-to-deployed, learn-loop, legacy-install, instruction-import</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/instructions-rule_guard">
        <rdfs:label>guard</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/InstructionsRule"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/instructions-rule_anchor">
        <rdfs:label>anchor</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/InstructionsRule"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>claude/CLAUDE.md, compose/instructions_catalog.py</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/guide_entityId">
        <rdfs:label>entityId</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Guide"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>guide</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:isIdentifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ont:isIdentifier>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/guide_routes">
        <rdfs:label>routes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Guide"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>author-to-deployed</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/guide_guard">
        <rdfs:label>guard</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Guide"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/guide_anchor">
        <rdfs:label>anchor</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Guide"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>claude/guides/*.md guide_id frontmatter</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/packaging-tier_entityId">
        <rdfs:label>entityId</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PackagingTier"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>packaging-tier</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:isIdentifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ont:isIdentifier>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/packaging-tier_routes">
        <rdfs:label>routes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PackagingTier"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>author-to-deployed</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/packaging-tier_guard">
        <rdfs:label>guard</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PackagingTier"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/packaging-tier_anchor">
        <rdfs:label>anchor</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PackagingTier"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>compose/domains.json tiers</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/domain_entityId">
        <rdfs:label>entityId</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Domain"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>domain</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:isIdentifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ont:isIdentifier>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/domain_routes">
        <rdfs:label>routes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Domain"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>author-to-deployed</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/domain_guard">
        <rdfs:label>guard</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Domain"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>gated</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/domain_anchor">
        <rdfs:label>anchor</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/Domain"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>compose/domains.json domains</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/payload-entry_entityId">
        <rdfs:label>entityId</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PayloadEntry"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>payload-entry</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:isIdentifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ont:isIdentifier>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/payload-entry_routes">
        <rdfs:label>routes</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PayloadEntry"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>author-to-deployed</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/payload-entry_guard">
        <rdfs:label>guard</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PayloadEntry"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>derived</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/payload-entry_anchor">
        <rdfs:label>anchor</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/PayloadEntry"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>package.json files[]</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/cli-subcommand_entityId">
        <rdfs:label>entityId</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/CliSubcommand"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>cli-subcommand</rdfs:comment>
        <ont:isIdentifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</ont:isIdentifier>
        <ont:propertyType>string</ont:propertyType>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://agent-bios.local/ontology/agent-bios/cli-subcommand_routes">
